{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And that which remains of the flesh and of the bread</b> — the bet in both words functions like a mem: 'from the flesh and from the bread.' And so too, 'on the eighth day and onward' (Ezekiel 43:27), 'in that year, eighteen years' (Judges 10:8). And Scripture did not specify 'and that which remains until morning' because the laws of the offerings had already been taught, and they knew that these shelamim are judged according to the most stringent among them, which are eaten for a day and a night. Or perhaps Scripture was brief here because it is explicitly stated in the command, 'And if any of the flesh of consecration and of the bread remains until morning' (Exodus 29:34)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:53.294154508Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}